// Regression (BUG#93): a module-qualified call to a module that is neither
// imported nor bundled must be a clean compile error, NOT a silent accept-then-
// miscompile. On the native textual-bundling path the resolver leaves such a
// `NODE_FIELD_EXPR` callee unresolved (flag 2048 unset), typecheck used to fall
// through leniently, and air_builder lowered the callee to a garbage register and
// emitted `call *reg` -> jump to an unmapped address -> SIGSEGV (exit 139) with no
// diagnostic. Same accept-then-miscompile class as BUG#53/#68/#88. Must reject.
fn main() -> i32:
    return std.nosuchmodule.frobnicate(1) as i32
